    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Significantly extended and enhanced to provide an impressive amount of living and bedroom space, this spacious three-bedroom semi-detached home was once a four bedroom house, which the current owners reconfigured to a 3-bedroom house to create an impressive master suite. The house combines generous family accommodation with a sunny south-west facing garden and an extensive attic conversion.\r\nOne of the standout features of Number 62 is the substantial two-storey extension completed in 2007. Designed to considerably increase the size and versatility of the original house, this major addition has created valuable extra living space at ground floor level together with additional bedroom accommodation upstairs.\r\nThe property’s main bedroom is particularly well appointed, benefitting from its own ensuite bathroom and walk-in wardrobe to create a comfortable and generously proportioned principal bedroom suite.\r\nFurther enhancing the accommodation is an extensive attic conversion spanning both the original and extended sections of the house. Currently used as additional accommodation, this substantial space is further complemented by its own ensuite bathroom, adding considerably to the flexibility of the property.\r\nAt the rear of the house, a bright and inviting sunroom enjoys a pleasing outlook over the back garden. This provides an attractive additional reception space and creates a natural connection between the house and garden.\r\nOutside, the sunny south-west facing back garden is another highlight. Landscaped with ease of maintenance in mind, it incorporates an inviting patio area providing an ideal setting for outdoor dining, summer barbecues, entertaining family and friends or simply relaxing in the afternoon and evening sun.\r\nThe garden also accommodates a large shed with an electricity supply. In addition to providing excellent storage, its size and power connection offer potential for a variety of alternative uses depending on the requirements of the new owners.\r\nTo the front, a large tarmac driveway provides generous off-street parking for up to three cars. The property has also benefitted from the installation of new windows and doors to the front of the house in 2022.\r\nWith its substantial two-storey extension, extensive attic conversion, main bedroom suite, excellent off-street parking and sunny south-west facing garden, Number 62 offers an exceptional amount of versatile living space and all the ingredients required for a comfortable modern family home.\r\nCall us today to arrange a viewing of this must-see property.\r\nLOCATION\r\nRichmond Park is a mature residential development offering the combination of a settled neighbourhood setting and convenient access to the shops, schools, transport links, sporting facilities and recreational amenities of the surrounding area.\r\nThe mature nature of the development, together with the generous proportions of established homes such as Number 62, makes Richmond Park particularly well suited to family living.\r\nEveryday needs are well catered for by a good selection of shops, supermarkets and services within easy reach, while the wider area provides a variety of cafés, restaurants and leisure amenities.\r\nFamilies benefit from access to a choice of primary and secondary schools, along with childcare and pre-school facilities, while a range of local sports clubs, parks and outdoor amenities provides plenty of opportunities for recreation.\r\nThe area is also well positioned for commuters, with convenient road and public transport connections providing access to surrounding towns, employment centres and Dublin.\r\nCombining a mature residential setting with excellent local amenities and transport connections, Richmond Park is a convenient and well-established location for families, couples and anyone seeking a spacious home within easy reach of day-to-day essentials."
      },
